    "body": "Thank you for opening an issue @ajihyf! 🙂 \r\n\r\n> Maybe using string substitution to remove the prefix '-' is better?\r\n\r\nThe trouble with this solution is that it wouldn't also work for bash. At this point, it may be simpler to instead just have the following in our installation instructions:\r\n\r\n#### Zsh\r\n\r\nAdd the following to the end of `~/.zshrc`:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n# ~/.zshrc\r\n\r\neval \"$(starship init zsh)\"\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### Fish\r\n\r\nAdd the following to the end of `~/.config/fish/config.fish`:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n# ~/.config/fish/config.fish\r\n\r\neval (starship init fish)\r\n```\r\n\r\n#### Bash\r\n\r\nAdd the following to the end of `~/.bashrc`:\r\n\r\n```sh\r\n# ~/.bashrc\r\n\r\neval \"$(starship init bash)\"\r\n```",
